---
/**
 * Controller details match naurra.ai's registered entity, taken from the
 * Organization schema in voice-ai-client/src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro so the
 * two sites cannot disagree about who operates them.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const updated = '9 August 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What Total Football collects, why, and how to have it deleted."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="shell max-w-prose py-20 md:py-28">
    <p class="micro mb-6">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="text-title font-black">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-faint">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 text-[16px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85">
      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black text-ink">The short version</h2>
        <p>
          Two things, and only two. Your email address, if you type it into a form. And a count of
          which pages get read, which contains nothing that identifies you and which you can switch
          off in one click. There are no cookies at all, no advertising trackers, and no
          third-party analytics scripts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black text-ink">Email, if you subscribe</h2>
        <p>
          We store your email address, the page or form you subscribed from, and the date. The
          source is recorded so we can tell which content is worth writing more of.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black text-ink">Analytics, and why there is no cookie banner</h2>
        <p>
          We count which pages get read so we know what to write next. There is no cookie banner
          because there are no cookies, and because nothing collected identifies you. You can switch
          the counting off in one click using
          <strong class="font-bold">Do not count my visit</strong> at the bottom of any page, and if
          your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal we obey it
          automatically without you doing anything.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">Each record contains:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
          <li>the page you viewed, and how long the tab was actually in front of you</li>
          <li>which links you clicked, where those leave the site or are a call to action</li>
          <li>the website that referred you, as a domain name only</li>
          <li>your country, and whether you are on mobile, tablet or desktop</li>
          <li>a random session identifier, described below</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Just as importantly, here is what is <strong class="font-bold">not</strong> recorded: no
          cookies of any kind, no IP address, no browser fingerprint, no full user-agent string, no
          name, and no identifier that survives your visit or follows you to another website.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The session identifier is a random number generated in your browser and held in session
          storage, which your browser erases when you close the tab. It exists so we can tell that
          three page views were one visit rather than three people. It cannot be used to recognise
          you if you come back, and it is never linked to your email address even if you subscribe.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Because no cookies are used, no device storage is read for tracking purposes, and no
          personal data is collected, the lawful basis is our legitimate interest in understanding
          which articles are worth writing. You can object at any time with the opt-out above.
          Analytics records are kept for 14 months and then deleted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black text-ink">Server logs</h2>
        <p>
          Our host processes standard server logs (IP address, user agent, requested URL) for
          security and abuse prevention, on the basis of legitimate interest. Those logs are not
          combined with your email address or with the analytics described above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black text-ink">Why, and on what basis</h2>
        <p>
          Your email is used to send the newsletter you asked for, and nothing else. The lawful basis
          is your consent, which you can withdraw at any time. We do not sell, rent or share the
          list.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black text-ink">Where it is stored</h2>
        <p>
          Subscriber records are held in Supabase (PostgreSQL). The site is hosted by Netlify. Both
          may process data outside your country; both operate under standard contractual clauses for
          transfers out of the EEA and UK.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black text-ink">How long</h2>
        <p>
          Until you unsubscribe, plus a short period to honour the unsubscribe. Every email carries a
          one-click unsubscribe link.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black text-ink">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask for a copy of what we hold about you, have it corrected, or have it deleted
          outright. Write to the address below and we will action it. If you are in the EEA or UK you
          also have the right to complain to your data protection authority.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black text-ink">Who runs this site</h2>
        <p>
          Total Football is operated by <strong class="font-bold">NAURRA AI LTD</strong>, a company
          registered in Cyprus, number HE 493756, at 10 Kyriakou Matsi, LILIANA COURT, 4th Floor,
          Nicosia 1082, Cyprus. NAURRA AI LTD is the data controller for everything described above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-black text-ink">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For anything on this page, including access and deletion requests, email
          <a
            href="mailto:athanasios@naurra.ai"
            class="font-semibold text-ink underline underline-offset-2">athanasios@naurra.ai</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
